[90570] = {
  "9057018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Even as Alliance, you will need to complete the quests 'Twilight Missive' , A Somber Sun , Captured Information and Interrogation from Salandria for this quest to show up for Taelia Fordragon Last edited by DeadlyTitan19 on 2026/04/02 (Patch 12.0.1)",
},

[90571] = {
  "9057118080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050The 2nd location is up above, not inside the building.",
  "Wowhead050Ok, what exactly are we suppose to do to \"scout\" the Devouring Citadel? I sat at the marker for roughly 5 minutes. Nothing happened, nothing changed. I traveled around, nothing happened nothing changed. I don't have a quest item to use to scout the area. Someone stated the 2nd location is up above... well, how do you complete the first location? There should be more information in the quest dialog as to what we're suppose to do. If it wasn't for the fact this is a campaign quest, I'd abandon it and move on. But. . . Edit: I just need to open my eyes. There are abilities on my primary bar while directing Ciphus. Ability 1 is Scry, which when I pressed that, completed the first location. Duh. Sometimes I feel like a clone. Last edited by Aerynsun8449 on 2026/02/28 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Don't go inside the building. Just keep flying in the direction you started but fly above the buildings looking for the scrying areas (button 1 when you reach them)",
  "Wowhead050use the scry button to do your thing...when you need to do the 2nd location keep jumping and fly above the building to reach it. annoying vauge quest is annoying.",
  "Wowhead050The thing can fly, Try jumping",
  "Wowhead050Just look at the map and fly to the questpoint near the ground. Click the button that highlights when you are at the little glowing orb. Fly to the next..",
},

[90573] = {
  "9057318080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Don't do this quest the long way - Don't collect Misplaced Tomes around the zone for Latent Arcana! TL;DR - Use the coins from from Lord Sathriel to get quests from the guests - The quests reward 25 Latent Arcana per quest = the 100 Latent Arcana required for the Runestone! Read my full comment on Fortify the Runestones: Blood Knights for details.",
  "Wowhead050The quest log recommends 5 people, but it appears to be soloable, with the boss scaling with players.",
  "Wowhead050Adding my experience: I charged the runestone to 80%ish, wasn't enough so I went away to farm some more, when I came back someone else charged the thing to 100% and I couldn't participate in the small event of killing mobs and then the final boss (I tried killing them anyway but it didn't count for me). Then I looked for another runestone to charge and someone charged it to 100% while I was close to it and this time the thing started for me too even though I didn't contribute at all. So I guess my take from this is: be close to the runestone when it gets to 100%.",
},

[90574] = {
  "9057418080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Don't do this quest the long way - Don't collect Coalesced Light orbs around the zone for Latent Arcana! TL;DR - Use the coins from from Lord Sathriel to get quests from the guests - The quests reward 25 Latent Arcana per quest = the 100 Latent Arcana required for the Runestone! In contrast to other comments, this was a very easy and quick quest to complete solo (except for the very final kill - read on). Each week you select a sub-faction from Lord Sathriel, two of which offer a bonus coin (this week for me it showed the bonus coin for Blood Knights and Shades of the Row, not sure if this changes week to week) You receive 3 coins by default, and an extra coin if you choose a faction with a bonus as above - This week, I chose Blood Knights, hence why I'm commenting on this quest. With each coin, you speak to the four faction representatives in the same area (they have progress bars above their heads), and offer them a coin. In return, they offer you a quest - Each quest rewards 25 Latent Arcana - 4 tokens (if you pick the bonus) = 100 Latent Arcana These quests are very simple kill/ collect quests around Eversong with minimal requirements. You take your 100 Latent Arcana rewarded from the 4 quests to a Runestone and repeatedly click the button in the popup window - 100 Latent Arcana = 100% progress bar on the Runestone Once the Runestone is at 100%, a heap of mobs will spawn, you kill a bunch of them to get another progress bar to 100% Everything has been easily and quickly solo-able so far Now an elite spawns - It is only for this final elite where a group would be handy, but in my case, there were a heap of players who happened to instantly turned up and it was all over in a few minutes.",
  "Wowhead050This is probably the hands down worst event ive done in wow in my 20 years of playing the game. Good job blizzard. Maybe this is supposed to be done as a group thing and i did it early in the morning so i had to charge these stones totally by my self, which takes AGES. For the record you have to collect those small yellow orbs around Eversong then go back to the runestone to charge it. One orb give you about 5% progress on the stone, and i think i have found one of these orbs every 10min or so. I will be humble and say that, maybe im just terrible at the game, but this is honestly just garbage quest/ event design imo. edit: i have since writing calmed down a bit, and this is infinitely easier when there are players around. TLDR: Dont try to do this event alone in the middle of the night is my tip to others. Last edited by Tasseq on 2026/03/04 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Fully powered the stone, defended the stone, even killed the boss. no credit.",
  "Wowhead050I didn't get credit for the quest after fully charging the runestone and killing all the mobs. It is possible that the tank tanked the elite too far from the runestone.",
  "Wowhead050For those of you like me who don't ever look at the map, to find the correct runestone, just open your map; it will be clearly marked, and it does rotate from site to site. Go there, activate it, and solo it, or start your own group; it'll fill super quick.",
  "Wowhead050I have the 100 latent arcana, where the heck is the runestone?",
  "Wowhead050Runestone locations: / way 47.36 58.64 Elrendar River Runestone / way 39.13 56.85 Ath'ran Runestone / way 57.70 53.59 Dawnstar Spire Runestone / way 41.15 73.81 Sanctum of the Moon Runestone / way 40.46 13.59 Sunstrider Isle Runestone (Thank you, yvsicle )",
},

[90575] = {
  "9057518080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Don't do this quest the long way - Don't collect Ranger's Caches around the zone for Latent Arcana! TL;DR - Use the coins from from Lord Sathriel to get quests from the guests - The quests reward 25 Latent Arcana per quest = the 100 Latent Arcana required for the Runestone! Read my full comment on Fortify the Runestones: Blood Knights for details.",
  "Wowhead050If the quest is bugged (runic stone stuck at 100%, and no way to start the event, since it seems to happen so many times...), try server hopping with the LFG tool, it's the only way if you can't wait days to complete.",
},

