[90724] = {
  "9072418080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050This quest does not exist for me to pick up. Cleared the raid tonight, used the \"quest\" option for return to Silvermoon, but there is no The Broken Sky for me to get. I did the full campaign and have Loremaster. Now, Feeding the Flame is the campaign quest showing up for me, which is a Horde chain and I'm Alliance. Bottom line: I show I completed The Voidspire (the / run print shows true), but have no way of picking up The Broken Sky . Update: It appears you have to complete the entire Feeding the Flame chain on each character for them to successfully progress each of their campaigns, despite already having completion of The Voidspire . I reran that entire chain and was able to pick up The Broken Sky . Last edited by Organick on 2026/03/26 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Rewards 10 Adventurer Crests that ignore the crest cap if you're already full for the week.",
  "Wowhead050I thought the quest was bugged because it kept teleporting me back to the area when I tried to leave. It turns out you just have to talk to magister umbric again and he has an option for you to leave.",
  "Wowhead050All those people. Our army. Our heroes. Our leaders. Gone. I'm...really confused. The last quest before this was Arator's parents arguing with each other about hurting Arator, surrounded by tents and active workers. After I finished that, the tents, workers, and Arator's parents just vanished. I didn't see a battle or anything explaining why. Now Arator just says everyone's gone...what happened? Did I miss a cinematic or something?",
},

