[91838] = {
  "9183818080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050The last orb is in the cave up north at 46.52, 37.59... took me a while to find it for some reason.",
  "Wowhead050If you care about the mount farm, this one gives the buff that stacks ten times. Reciprocal Power Size increased by 10%. Damage dealt increased by 5%. Periodically heals for 8% every 2 sec. for 5 min 5 minutes remaining and provides an NPC that does a ton of damage, so avoid turning this in if you want to keep the buff in the area and the NPC. Last edited by tweaklet on 2026/03/12 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050in cave / way 46.52, 37.59",
},

[91839] = {
  "9183918080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050No parsed comments available yet. Wowhead URL: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=91839",
},

[91840] = {
  "9184018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Frostmourne OCE 1/ 03/ 26 - Bugged stuck at 1HP. Moved to Warmode and was able to kill her.",
  "Wowhead050Hey. When I arrived at the location where I was supposed to kill the NPC, she wasn't there and nothing was happening. I had War Mode enabled. I went back to the capital city to turn it off, returned to the location, and the NPC was there — quest completed successfully. Don't forget to turn War Mode back on afterwards. You can use your Personal Key to the Arcantina for that, it only has a 90-second cooldown :)",
  "Wowhead050I was able to complete this by switching into War Mode. I was initially not in War Mode, and she was not there. I waited for a very long time, she would not spawn. I hearthed, switched to War Mode, and went back. She was there.",
  "Wowhead050This NPC can bug and get stuck at 1hp during the roleplay that is triggered at the end of the fight. Hop shards and restart the encounter to fix.",
  "Wowhead050Didn't get the 1% bug (though it did take a while to trigger) but oddly, I was really close to the NPC when it finally triggered and somehow it turned my character invisible. Reloading didn't fix it, and I had to relog. Never seen that one before.",
  "Wowhead050Enabling warmode fixed this for me as well. 3/ 20/ 26",
},

[91843] = {
  "9184318080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Bugged Quest I submitted a bug report I couldn’t move or hearth or even close my game. Had to use an alternative method to close out the game. Dang it!",
  "Wowhead050If you get bugged do not restart, it takes to right back to the beginning. I was trapped in Tazavesh (door was closed and wouldn't open - even after relog and reloadui). And not restarting it... it can do one!",
},

[91863] = {
  "9186318080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050No parsed comments available yet. Wowhead URL: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=91863",
},

[91864] = {
  "9186418080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050i have already done all this, this is the most awful questline in wow history, i feel like trapped and punished in a scenario that never ends",
  "Wowhead050This quest would be a good quest if it was just a re-\"CAP\", not a re-\"DO\" of quest line's we have already completed. Mabey like 3 video, one for the beginning, middle, and end, with voice overs explaining what happen in TWW. not this redo of old quests.",
  "Wowhead050This is torture. Why we must suffer like this? I thought its going to be bunch of important cutscenes. Nope. You get to do ALL the boring quests, AGAIN.",
  "Wowhead050If you need to \"consult the tome\" and can't see the button for it because you dared make your minimap slightly larger than normal just enter the game's edit mode and drag the minimap to the side or make it smaller Then you can see the hyper-specific \"consult the tome\" button and press it No idea why they chose to put it on top of the UI quest list but there it is",
  "Wowhead050Holy hell we already did all of this, how do you skip it?",
  "Wowhead050Not worth it. It is not a recap, it's basically forcing you to redo a large portion of the starter quests of the expansion.",
  "Wowhead050Please fix this questline... no one needs to do this, and I'm stuck and can't pick up any other quests or get credit for World Quests. So frustrating that you can't abandon this questline to get rid of it smh.",
  "Wowhead050After helping in the Freywold, fly back to Dornogal to find the Tome at the Foundation Hall stairs.",
  "Wowhead050There is a big RED X on the upper right corner to get out of this waste of time.",
  "Wowhead050Absolutely FFFFFFFF this. I already did all of this and tried to abandon it but I can't. I can't do other things because this questline causes you to be phased to the rest of the game even if it appears normal. As an example, I couldn't do a sky riding daily as the game was falsely informing me was no room in my bags and I apparently didn't meet the requirements for a quest I've done many times before. Every single thing they do makes me want to quit. This whole quest line is taking me HOURS. It so buggy and I can't get out of it. Super annoyed. Last edited by FlexoAdapt on 2025/12/17 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050DO NOT START THIS! thought it going to be a recap like the lorewalker cho bits, but it actually just makes you do the whole storyline.",
  "Wowhead050Just give us the F'ing bag of gear!",
  "Wowhead050If you open the book and the press the X to leave, you return to Dornogal. And if you talk again with the book, you have the option to \"Continue\" where you left. (Do not abandon the quest). Anyway I'm stuck at the \"Consult the Tome to learn about the Highspeaker's reaction\". So for now, I think the best is: do NOT abandon the quest and wait for Blizzard to fix this step.",
  "Wowhead050Seriously, what is this? I've done all this already!",
  "Wowhead050I'm stuck on the last step Aid the Bronzebeards confronting the Highspeaker Magni saved everyone and turned back to fleshmode but the step isn't completed and there's nobody to turn in the quest.",
  "Wowhead050I can't figure out where I'm supposed to be -- I feel like I've hit a bug somewhere. It says, \"Speak with Merrix and aid the earthen in Freywold.\" I went to Freywold and helped put the people in the pool and got the cut scene of the neurbians flying over but now... nothing? I can't get anything else to pop up and the book is doing literally nothing.",
  "Wowhead050After you do the Rookery with the followers select \"Teleport Out of Dungeon.\" Then open map and you'll see the \"?\" on how to proceed. Merrix will be at on the outskirts of The Coreway. Very frustrating how Blizzard is so extremely vague as where and what to do at times.",
  "Wowhead050POST PATCH EDIT: Appears to be fixed after an update. The Tome teleports you to the Ringing Deeps 42.5 10.2 and offers the option 'I wish to learn what the Highspeaker did.' allowing you to progress. On a side note, it appears they also fixed the disconnect loop I suffered on multiple characters after flying into the Ringing Deeps on the Tome from Dornogal. FINAL EDIT: After abandoning and a complete REDO, the Tome appeared to me in the house around the corner from the flight path in Gundargaz and allowed me to complete the quest. I'm almost 80 now so I'm moving on. Again, good luck friends. EDIT: WARNING: Abandoning the quest at this point makes you redo the entire quest line. I'm currently back at Aid the forces of Dalaran. Good luck, friends. EDIT: I am (was) at 0/ 1 Consult the Tome to learn about the Highspeaker's reaction. Quest Text: Consult the Tome of History to learn about the fate of Dalaran in The War Within. Consulting the Tome gives the following choice: <Close the Tome of History> After traveling back to Dornogal and finding the Tome at 49.5 31.8 I am given the option of: (Teleport) I'm a little lost. Where does this part of the story take place, again? After selecting my only option, I am immediately teleported back to the Ringing Deeps just to relive my original dilemma of being told to consult the Tome with only an option of closing the Tome. Submitting ticket and going outside to touch snow. Any helpful comments below would be appreciated. Last edited by Umbric on 2025/12/04 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050Okay, like everyone else I absolutely hated doing all of this. BUT.... I did find scenes that were eliminated from the original walk through of the opening segments that were NEW here. I would hazard a guess that Blizzard made more than they originally needed but decided to give it to us here at the end. It was a good way to remind us of things that had happened but also to show us the void story again which is only going to get bigger in Midnight. Do it before you pick up the story line from Arator and you pick up the conversation nicely. There is a nice payoff for going straight into the those quests. Take an afternoon.. It's taken me over 4 because I did stop and watch every cutscene. If you get lost, and the story just drops, the tome is not there ... and it does happen... just hearth home and go back to the tome and talk with it again. Do all of this on your main or even better a enchanter so they can disenchant everything you get and just do it. Thankful for Warbands AGAIN! Once I started this, I COULD NOT do anything else. No world quests, nothing.. I could craft and go to my home, but that's it.",
  "Wowhead050For anyone stuck on Aid the Machine Speakers in the deeps, after the High Speaker has spoken, go to the flight path in Gundargaz, enter the building at 42.96, 33.89 and the next quest step will appear with Speaker Brinthe.",
  "Wowhead050So I'm doing this quest not as a returner but to hurry up leveling a 70 to 80 toon I'd ignored. Observations only: It would be lovely to be able to escape the grind of the quest chain when reaching 80 But that might cause problems - see other comments All quests become available after completing this storyline (before picking up \"where the light touches\") But you may need to reload ui or relog to get them to show up (or do a timewalking dungeon to pass the time) Last edited by arednie on 2025/12/04 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050as. of 1/ 17/ 26. this quest can not be completed. Helping Dalaran forces never completes",
  "Wowhead050I agree with everyone who says this isn't worth doing, but I did it anyway. I had to abandon and restart because I had a break between doing the Rookery Follower dungeon and the next step, which requires you to turn it in to Merrix at / way 35.92, 52.56 . If you go back to the Book, you're stuck.",
  "Wowhead050Do NOT abandon the questline! it will make you begin back at square one up in Dalaran no matter how far into the recap you got.",
  "Wowhead050For anybody that is stuck on this, opening the tome from the speech bubble next to the red X to exit fixed it for me. I had to use the Tome to teleport back to the Meadery even though i'd completed that stage of the quest, then i could follow on to the coreway and the quest into the deeps.",
},

[91868] = {
  "9186818080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050I'm stuck on both \"Return to Dornogal\" and the part \"Consult the Tome to learn more about Arathis fight\", logging in or out doesn't solve it nor does abandoning the quests. Hours wasted </ 3 Update: I tried the whole questline again on an alt since 12.0.0 update, and it worked flawlessly, so it seems to be fixed :) Last edited by elzahra on 2026/02/09 (Patch 12.0.0)",
  "Wowhead050Got stuck: couldn't turn in, mount up, log off, or exit game. Exited Recap and was able to pick it up again and complete it at the Tome in Pornogal.",
  "Wowhead050Im stuck on \"Consult the Tome to learn more about Arathis fight\" even when relogging, or picking up quest again. Any ideas? Last edited by Conzec89 on 2025/12/03 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050I was stuck on this too. Twice through - no Tome appeared, dropped the quest, started again same results. Then I noticed that there is a RECAP bar above your objectives on the right side of your screen. The little yellow speech bubble lets you 'consult the tome'. Doesn't matter if you can see the tome or not - consult it and proceed in the storyline.",
  "Wowhead050Having trouble completing this? Open the quest log while you have the recap quest active and abandon it. Not via the book but the journal-menu. Edit: Be sure to look for the Recap bar above your quest objectives list in your UI. Last edited by Lanois on 2026/01/19 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050I'm stuck at \"Aid Alleria, Anduin, and Faerin. It keeps telling me that I don't meet the requirements for the dungeon. I'm a level 80 character.",
  "Wowhead050im stuck in the quest \" Return to Dornogal \" went i move to Dornogal Merrixx is not there and i can't continue the story.",
  "Wowhead050For new and returning players that are stuck at RECAP “Return to Dornogal”. This is because you have not completed the quest line in the traditional way. You need to completely drop the recap. Then go through the entire storyline beginning with the intro quest at Silithus. Once you finish the first chapter, you’ll be able to fly in, and port in and out of Dornogal.",
  "Wowhead050A temporary workaround for the bug where you are unable to speak to Merrix, until Blizzard resolves the issue: You need to go to Silithus and progress a few questlines in the regular campaign, ending with the The First Blow questline. You must complete the final quest ( Recompense ) in the The First Blow questline. After this, Merrix should no longer be phased, and you should be able to turn in the Return to Dornogal quest. This process may take a little time, and some of the recap quests will need to be completed again. However, my girlfriend and I were able to complete them within an hour. Hope this helps :) Last edited by Virus2001 on 2025/12/09 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050I'm stuck at \"Aid Alleria, Anduin, and Faerin\" after previously being stuck at \"Return to Dornogal\". The Workaround for Return to Dornogal was to run the full campaign back to a certain point to unlock Merrix. Then it got stuck again at this point and I haven't found a workaround for that yet. I did Exit the recap and try again from the Dornogal Tome, my character ends up just stuck behind the Tome in this case and there's no progression. So that doesn't work. Catch Up has been buggy for a lot of folks and blizz doesn't seem to care.",
  "Wowhead050Still happening on 12.0.1. Got stuck twice, at different points. The last time at the Consult the tome like other comments suggests. Nothing fixed it for me. I'm not doing it a 3rd time. This beign still buggy is nuts... I'm dropiing it sadly.",
  "Wowhead050Still bugged. I managed to do the entire quest, but once I was done I realized I never got credit for the step \"Consult with the Tome of History on the crash in Azj-Kahet\". Is there really no workaround?",
  "Wowhead050Para los que se han quedado atascados, solo no se adelanten a nada, el libro los lleva siempre al lugar donde deberían estar para iniciar o completar la misión, en la sub tarea \"Consulta el Tomo para saber más sobre la lucha de Arathi.\" esperen a que el libro termine de contar la historia y los teletransportara al poblado de Mereldar, no se adelanten volando por que entonces la subtarea no queda completa y tendrán que reiniciar la misión que inicia Cristalia.",
},

[91871] = {
  "9187118080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050When I get to the part \"Consult the Tome about Locus-Walker's summons to Tazavesh\" I click the Consult the Tome button but all I get is \"Target is not on the ground\". Tried to teleport to Dornogal and I get \"Can't do that while moving\". Tried to logout and I get \" You can't logout now\". Why Blizzard why? Anyone have any idea? I don't want to exit recap after doing all this. Update: Ok never mind. I alt F4 and logged back in and Consult the Tome worked finally. Last edited by SweetTea123 on 2026/01/11 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050I conquered Dimensius, watched the full post battle video for this raid, but receive zero guidance from the Tome on how to finish aiding Alleria. I tried consulting the Tome, but that didn't help, I tried quitting the Tome, exiting the game and reopening the Tome activity again, but ZERO guidance from the Tome. Any idea on how to complete aiding Alleria story line or is it bugged? At this point, I am just redoing the whole campaign, which is annoying, but it has helped level up another of my characters.",
  "Wowhead050WARNING: I got through the Dimensius raid event and accidentally selected 'take me back to where I started' instead of talking to NPC to exit storyline raid and it put me in Orgrimmar with no possible way to return to the RECAP even by exiting and taking it back up. Be careful not to ever select 'take me back...' from the tome because you will have no choice but to completely re-run 2 hours of progress.",
  "Wowhead050This quest line probably have more bugs than I've previously encountered combined over 20+ years.",
  "Wowhead050The items in the Worldsoul Satchel are currently bugged and starting at 400, however they do upgrade as regular s3 TWW Explorer, so 2/ 8 turns them into 645 . The Valor cost for this has been supplied by the quest chain (Dimensius quest cache included).",
  "Wowhead050In case this happens to anyone else: I killed Dimensius, but before I could click on the portal, my game crashed. When I got back in, I wasn't in the raid anymore and I didn't have Manaforge quest. I went back to the raid, and still nothing. I logged out and back in, and still nothing. I decided to hearth back to Dorn, and when I loaded I had the quest again and it was complete. So, if something similar happens to you, just get to Dorn and you should be good.",
  "Wowhead050I had the problem that I couldn't summon the Tome of History after the first Undermine cinematic, with the error message \"Couldn't find the Tome on the ground\", or something like that. I couldn't log out or exit game properly, and had to alt-F4. I logged in again and it worked. So if you encounter this problem, simply alt-F4 and log in again, easy peasy :)",
  "Wowhead050I think the final bag is bugged, I got item level 400 gear while sporting 545 ilvl gear from the long quest chain.",
  "Wowhead050It did not work for me to complete it after finishing Dimensius. Eventually I went on another char and did the campaign (no recap) and then I came back on main , dropped the recap and everything was unlocked. I kept reading that you do need to do the campaing on one char for the recap to work.",
  "Wowhead050I am at \"Aid Xal'atath and Ve'nari\" and I'm not sure HOW I'm supposed to do that? No indication on map as to where. The Tome drops me into that theatre in Tazavesh where we killed Azir. The only NPCs there are Alleria, Xala'atath and Locus Walker - and none has any quest text to provide hints. Prior quest item says \"Consult the tome to learn about the search for more ribbons.\" As I completed (except for the raid) the Ka'resh storyline, I went to the locations in Ka'resh where I remember getting more ribbons (i.e., off that dead person in the Naresh dome that was hit by an asteroid and in the main dome where we talk to those Ka'reshi priests), but no joy. Can anyone help me? I'd like to get through this on one toon so I can (hopefully) skip this on others.",
  "Wowhead050Can someone plz help me first i got stuck inside the building, heart out en have flight to the guilding landing i see the npc's but cant start the coversation for dimensius, already have done the storyline for the second time and always end up here stuck",
  "Wowhead050Tips from my own runthrough: If you get stuck in the building when you're supposed to go to the docks, hearth out then take the portal in the Dornogal throne room to Tazavesh and then fly to the docks. Before you start the raid, make sure you are in dynamic flight mode and not steady flight. Steady flight is too slow. When you start flying the dragon, make sure you go through the rings and use your dynamic flight speed up action as much as possible. If you do not make it to the platform before your co-raiders kill the mob, Dimensius will one-shot you. Last edited by Kushana on 2026/01/28 (Patch 12.0.0)",
  "Wowhead050Finally happened to me. On my 7th 80 I took the portal at the end and then the game crashed and I was DCed. Can't complete the Storyline for the end reward. I tried everything. Ended up just dropping it and won't be finishing it. Not slogging through all that again when I have a few more classes to level and do this all over again... and again... Wish they would fix it. Edit: Just after I posted this and had dropped the quest I said screw it and repicked it back up and did Continue instead of Start Over. Was able to complete the quest and finish the Recap. On to character #8! Last edited by Coronus on 2026/02/23 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050I got stuck on the very final quest (\"Aid Alleria in the defeat of Dimensius\"), like many others. I could not work out how to complete the quest after defeating Dimensius in story-mode. I finally cracked it - you have to loot the boss and you will pick up an item that starts a quest. Once you've left the raid, click the quest in your quest log to turn it in. The tome will appear and you can finish the chain.",
},

[91872] = {
  "9187218080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Make sure to do the campaign quest up until the moment you 'awake' in this town. The Former Rootwarden will become available then.",
  "Wowhead050Appears that you need to have One Does Not Simply Walk Into Harandar completed to see the storylines: A Goblin in Harandar Cultivating Hope Bloomtown I saw them at level 88 after completing the main story of Harandar",
  "Wowhead050If you're doing adventure mode, make sure to pick up the Harandar quest from the Scouting table in Silvermoon. You'll need to do the first couple of quests from the main questline and then it'll take you right to Hagar once you finish the delve through the story.",
  "Wowhead050Really odd that there are no special dialogue for Night Elves during this questline.",
  "Wowhead050If you dont see this quest, you just need progress some quests in location :)",
},

[91873] = {
