[91986] = {
  "9198618080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050You have to wait for their 'disoriented' debuff to fall off before you can successfully use the item on the mobs. Super cool as it's a 3 minute debuff and people are camping around waiting to tag one.",
  "Wowhead050Swapped to war mode and got this done in a couple minutes (after unsuccessfully trying to do it out of wm).",
  "Wowhead050\"Drive 8 Daggerspine Snapdragons mad with a tune\". Ironic, because this quest turns us the player absolutely mad.",
  "Wowhead050Nice quest blizzard.",
  "Wowhead050What a terrible quest design.",
  "Wowhead050Who ever designed this piece of madness should be fired alongside the ones who approved of it...",
  "Wowhead050Using the item on the snapdragons does not dismount you.",
  "Wowhead050Please have the decency to kill the mob after you use it, instead of just leaving it untaggable for everyone else.",
  "Wowhead050Do not kill the Snapdragon. Target it and use the quest item. You can't do it if someone else hit them first or they're in combat from what I can tell. Also randomly doesn't work for some other weird reason. Last edited by Belazriel on 2026/03/02 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050The item was not working for me at all. Relog fixed it.",
  "Wowhead050Worst quest in the expansion so far. Impossible to get done when other players are around. Was this designed in a vacuum?",
  "Wowhead050Item works in stealth without breaking it and even if the target is tagged by the enemy faction. Just make sure the damn beast is not \"confused\"!",
  "Wowhead050Using the quest item doesn't break stealth. Makes it much easier to complete.",
  "Wowhead050It feels better to camp a spawn point than to fly around, for me at least. Respawn seems to be about 3 minutes.",
},

[91987] = {
  "9198718080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050The mob you're looking for is Lightbloom Lasher. They're small, spawn in groups of 3, and as of writing seem to have a pretty bad spawn rate on live. Usually only drops 1 bulb per group as well. Took me maybe 15 minutes to complete.",
  "Wowhead050The quest has a large targeted zone to the south but I had zero luck finding the mobs there on live. There's a second area to the far east near Suncrown Village - was able to complete the quest within a minute or two after going there, plenty of mobs.",
  "Wowhead050Fly around and spam this: / targetexact Lightbloom Lasher / ping [@target] Don't know why health bars don't show unless you are very close.",
  "Wowhead050The macro should be: / targetexact Lightbloom Lasher / ping [@target,nodead] otherwise it will target every dead mob and ping them.",
  "Wowhead050If this quest isn't tracking or isn't dropping for you on Live relog. I had to relog twice before the lashers in the quest area started dropping the bulbs. (Note the bulbs don't have the best drop rate either so an easy way to tell if it is working now is to check the tooltip on the mobs.)",
  "Wowhead050You are looking for Invasive Prismonia . They are tiny little plant elementals and spawn in the smaller (=eastern) quest area. They come in packs of three and drop 1 quest item per pack. There's probably also some mobs in the larger area, but I couldn`t find any. Maybe overfarmed, maybe a horrible spawn rate, or maybe another bug in this official Midnight release version, that feels like a Beta.",
  "Wowhead050The macro should be: / targetexact Lightbloom Lasher / ping [@target,nodead] otherwise it will target every dead mob and ping them. Last edited by cybercowboy82 on 2026/03/17 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050You'll definitely benefit from using a macro while doing this quest.",
},

[91988] = {
  "9198818080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050There is a bright berry in your inventory you use on the lil flying bro",
},

[91989] = {
  "9198918080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050\"Make sure to wash your hands before you rub your eyes... or worse. I learned this the hard way\" What did she mean by this?",
  "Wowhead050Ghostland Peppers are in the tranquil Repose area, starting at approx. 44 - 72 south of the pond",
},

[91990] = {
  "9199018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050The sea caller to call the slugs is in your bags.",
  "Wowhead050The quest item Sea Caller can be used while mounted. You do not need to fight a single naga for this quest. Just run around and use the item. Last edited by pmakaro on 2026/04/02 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050You can use the item without breaking stealth.",
  "Wowhead050You can use the flute while mounted.",
},

[91991] = {
  "9199118080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050It's not the bottles or grapes on the platforms. On ground level against post fence.. blue barrel. 40, 61 Last edited by Jkizis on 2026/03/26 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050No options to click the wine... any ideas?",
},

[91993] = {
  "9199318080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Upon using the wand, your target will either immediately shrink down and be captured or turn hostile. Once the target is hostile, there is nothing you can do to then capture it. I had a string of at least 10 in a row where everything was just going hostile before they started capturing for me. JUST KEEP TRYING.",
  "Wowhead050Annoying quest. 5/ 6 will agro. Takes forever.",
  "Wowhead050I thought this quest was annoying the first time i did it, but like someone else mentioned - if you mount up when the wand cast bar is almost done (which doesn't interrupt the cast), you can just fly up and then back down and avoid having to fight the frog. rinse and repeat by zapping the same frog until it turns green... it saves a lot of time and this quest becomes quite easy Last edited by Tagazin on 2026/03/16 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050I was on my hunter as BM and as soon as I dismiss my pets it start working",
  "Wowhead050I dropped this quest, after every single toad in the area was hostile, life's too short for this",
  "Wowhead050Blue frogs worked for me, yellow frogs were angry frogs!",
  "Wowhead050On top of the usual, this quest is even more annoying when there's a void strike/ attack on the Gates of SMC. Coz yeah, the toads are fighting the mobs, which respawn fast. Last edited by concordantnexus 6 days ago (Patch 12.0.5)",
  "Wowhead050Seems like the first two, then about one in three thereafter will attack you rather than allow themselves to be captured. Poison dispel helps.",
  "Wowhead050I found that only the red frogs would shrink for me. The yellow/ brown ones all turned hostile. Hope that helps someone!",
  "Wowhead050What worked for me was removing my armor (basically getting \"naked\") so I wouldn’t trigger any extra auto-attacks. If a toad turned hostile, I used a speed buff to outrun it instead of killing it.",
  "Wowhead050Here is the video guide if you are having trouble completing this quest. https:// youtu.be/ u7GnpIrvjvk",
  "Wowhead050CC them first. Root, sap, poly... That way you can just run away when they aggro, way faster than killing them.",
},

[91995] = {
  "9199518080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050If a Void Strike is up in the area when you go to do this quest, you can still get it done, but you have to go to the south side of the quest area where the void strike does not overlap with it. I found two Daggerspine Infuser s there, which respawned quickly.",
},

