[92162] = {
  "9216218080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Official launch date and we already have a winner for the 'worst world quest of the expansion\" award.",
  "Wowhead050Stone to start it is at: 37.52 47.77",
  "Wowhead050I do not enjoy this quest. I am frequently flying around too far and getting kicked out of the WQ area.",
  "Wowhead050Maybe just a bug I happened to encounter but I found as a druid in flight form if you interact with the stone the game will still have you in \"flight form\" while possessing the Potad, allowing you to simply jump and glide into the bugs like you were flying in flight form. Possible it could work with other mounts that transform you, though I haven't tested.",
  "Wowhead050If you're a druid, just stay in your flight form when you start this wq. Then, when you jump, you're basically just skyriding and you can complete it in seconds.",
  "Wowhead050I found that instead of jumping in a forward arc to try and hit the flying creatures, it is easier to be underneath them and slightly off side and then jump up. I hit a creature almost every time using this method.",
  "Wowhead050You start with 3 \"jumps\". Every time you fly through a floating bug, you will see a green splash animation and you get another jump. It goes straight up, I found. Last edited by wowqueen on 2026/03/02 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050I was trying to maintain 'flight' by constantly jumping, spinning, and reangling - this strat is very hard. I found it much easier to just line my character up with a bug while on the ground and launch myself and get 1 or 2 at a time and land and go again.",
  "Wowhead050I was expecting the worst going in to this one after reviewing the prior comments. For me, it was no big deal. I had one instance of being dismounted and as result having to go back to he Ancient Waystone to change back to needed form, but even with that, I had the quest done in about 2 minutes. Perhaps there was a fix during maintenance yesterday to correct whatever the pains were previously?",
  "Wowhead050The map listed this as \"Den of Echoes\". I had to fly down into a 'cave' area inside. You get turned into a beast of some kind and you get a vehicle bar. You then have to 'jump' to tag the creatures flying around. YMMV on how much fun this is.",
  "Wowhead050Concussion Simulator 2026.",
  "Wowhead050If you're on the main storyline quest chain Of Caves and Cradles, you won't be able to morph into the creature necessary for this quest. Finish or drop that quest chain and then it works without issue.",
  "Wowhead050I found, not maybe best way but helpfull, use Stylish Black Parasol . Use it, then click the stone. Now the trick. You need to remove form, and stay with 2 skills from it. So i did by turning around, jumping toward west 'exit', when you are near, game should remove the form but not the skills, but you cant jump to far, just turn around, back toward cave center, again when it does. So you should have the skills and your parasol on you. So now when you jump, i used jump twice to be a bit higher, when i was lower parasol didnt worked, you'll glide with it, giving you some control over where to go, and a bit easier way to finish the quest. Hope this help, it surely helped me, i hate that quest :)",
  "Wowhead050Currently bugged, I believe because of the 12.0.5 ? The \"phasing\" doesn't happen (at least for me) so I just get turned into the orange frog and none of the \"bee\" things appear. The usual mobs are all stilll there and just kill you while you're transformed.",
  "Wowhead050Insanely stupid, good feedback already on where to go etc, only tip is to get underneath a bug before you hop, at least that guarentees you one hit and you might grab others on the way down. Try not to bounce yourself out of the cavern or you'll need to go back to the stone to transform and will be chased by mobs.",
  "Wowhead050So you're basically a frog, propelling himself with farts. I'm down.",
  "Wowhead050This quest really isn't as bad as others are claiming. Just click on the Mural Stone, turn into a little creature, then jump in an arching movement, hitting the flying creatures above. Just make sure you're jumping towards the center, or you'll go out of bounds and turn back to normal form. If there are hostile mobs there, then you'll have to fly and click the Mural Stone again. This quest is actually really easy.",
  "Wowhead050zero issues. just jump forward a little before and ur fine. u can spam jump",
  "Wowhead050I dunno about you all but I found this to be really easy.",
},

[92163] = {
  "9216318080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050It's not showing up for me, and i'm already done with the main storyline",
  "Wowhead050This quest became available after I had completed the quest, Den of Nalorakk: Unforgiven . It likely becomes unavailable once any of these quests: \"Murloc Madness\", \"Fish are Food, not Friends,\" and \"Following Suit\" are completed. Update: It seems on subsequent characters, that this quest became available immediately when entering the village (in the story). Either the requirements were changed, or something else has happened here. Last edited by Syrieal on 2026/03/09 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Not Showing Up For Me, And I Have Done Den of Nalorakk: Unforgiven. Ran code / run print(C_QuestLog.IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(91958)) And it came back true. Have Tried Reloading/ Relogging, Deleting Wow Cache And Restarting My PC. The NPC Old Teo'zan Is There At / way #2437 46.0 65.0 Old Teo'zan . But There Is No Quest To Accept. Last edited by Fubar187421 on 2026/03/01 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Quest does not appear for me. Relogged, went completely out of the game, same results. Hopefully this bug is fixed during the actual release.",
  "Wowhead050Didn't show for me as well but I could enter the storyline at King Mrgl-Mrgl with the quests he gave me. So just go to / way #2437 52.8 60.2 King Mrgl-Mrgl and talk to him. Last edited by Rizzoh on 2026/03/14 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050This showed up for me after I completed Den of Nalorakk: Unforgiven and hit Renown 5.",
},

