[92365] = {
  "9236518080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050I got a bit confused, thinking I was supposed to go earn some currency or other elsewhere. But completing the quest is very quick and easy: - Find a chest, Selune's Stormarion Cores , in the nearby building. - Pick up 20 Selune's Stormarion Core from the chest. - Walk outside to a glowing circle and click the Extra Action Button to create two more glowing circles nearby. - At each of the two placeholders, spend 10 Cores on a defense of some kind. - Go back to Null-Theorist Selune to turn it in. / way #2405 25.8 68.7 Selune's Cores / way #2405 25.3 69.0 Create Defenses",
  "Wowhead050NPC is standing outside in plain view at 26.4, 67.5. If you can't see her, or the quest Creating Defenses, it's because she's also the quest giver for a daily (blue quest), which supersedes the [yellow] quest. You can / target her, but you won't see the NPC clearly if she's offering the daily. Go to the coords, see her standing beside Xy'dax, and click her anyway, even if it looks like she only offers a blue ! . Talking to her, you'll see she offers the quest.",
  "Wowhead050Quest is a bit hidden is handed out by the same NPC named \"Null-Theorist selune\" that gives weekly quest named Hidey-Hole Last edited by Strawberrymuffin on 2026/03/07 (Patch 12.0.1)",
},

[92390] = {
  "9239018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050The info above for location is wrong. This NPC is at: / way 39.75, 84.18 IN SLAYER'S RISE NOT VOIDSTORM",
  "Wowhead050Quest starts at / way 39.75, 84.17 in Master's Perch",
  "Wowhead050Confirmed- Master's perch. 39,84 Why aren't ALL the side quests marked on the map?",
},

[92396] = {
  "9239618080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Starts right outside the main gates of Silvermoon. Handed by Terel Bloodfate . Might help if you're just seeing that this quest is available in Silvermoon but no indicator as to where it starts. Last edited by flaicher on 2026/02/26 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050OUTSIDE OF CITY! The quest NPC that starts this quest is at / way 50.15, 34.24 Last edited by Xozus on 2026/02/27 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Even though the quest shows on the map \"inside\" of Silvermoon, the quest can be started outside of the gates of Silvermoon. Talk to Terel Bloodfate at / way 50.12, 34.21",
  "Wowhead050This quest was showing up as a low level quest. Some of the chain was showing normal other parts were low level. If you cant find it try turning on low level quests. location above are correct / way #2395 50.13 34.24 Terel Bloodfate",
  "Wowhead050For me the npc was at / way #2395 50.2 34.2 Terel Bloodfate",
  "Wowhead050/ way Eversong Woods:Quel'Thalas 50.12 34.23 'Terel Bloodfate '",
  "Wowhead050The quest marker for is buggy or phased a bit by its existence on the border of the city map and the Eversong Woods map and sometimes doesn't appear in either until you get close to the city gate.",
  "Wowhead050He is outside the south main gates... he is at the coord listed but outside the gates. starts with the quest Calling in the Cavalry. Somehow the coord show on TomTom the same... go figure. ;) Good Luck!",
  "Wowhead050Game map is stuck on old city location data.. someone wasn't paid enough to change this one. using addon MapCoords, Midnight 50.1 34.2 Last edited by Kilrathi3 on 2026/04/14 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050This is for anyone who's been unlucky enough to have TomTom routing the posted coordinates to north Silvermoon by the docks, where shockingly no NPC is located! This is the wrong location! Terel Bloodfate is on the left side of the south gates of Silvermoon as you stand facing them. Last edited by Vallista on 2026/03/02 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050The quest icon didnt appear because it was a low level quest? They may fix this soon",
},

[92402] = {
  "9240218080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050You will get an encounter bar that will fill up as you get closer to the crystals. They (most) glow pretty well, so should not be too hard to see. They look like the mana crystals from Legion. If you watch the screen closely, right after you click on the first one you find, there will be a little wisp that guides you to the next crystal. Some are hidden under bushes so they can be harder to see the glow. Last edited by curledlizard on 2026/01/21 (Patch 12.0.0)",
  "Wowhead050For Alliance, just take flight to Brumewood Hollow area and use the locator.",
},

[92407] = {
  "9240718080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050While You cast your extra button spell, you can mount and it will still finish casting, just don't move, and then you will fly away leaving any mobs that will spawn from the anomalies. Saves couple seconds of your time ;p Last edited by TomiOmit on 2026/03/18 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050On my UI, when the event is active, the quest disappears from the tracker, you actually need to click on the provided item called Anomaly Inverter in order to collapse the holes.",
  "Wowhead050They are like black-holes around the event area. You cannot complete it in raid.",
  "Wowhead050There should be a thing in your bags for this",
},

[92408] = {
  "9240818080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050I'm disappointed in this quest. They build it up to something meaningful and yet it fails to deliver. There is no backstory other than Gaari somehow got this cloak from some blood elf who shall remain unnamed and we don't know how, why or what the circumstances of their relationship was. C'mon, blizz, stop being so lazy like this. I was just starting to find it interesting by the time it ended. And before anyone comments, yes, I understand it's not integral to the main plot, but we have had many other quests exactly like this that found a resolution and gave you a good story. Last edited by Jeolene on 2026/03/21 (Patch 12.0.1)",
},

[92417] = {
  "9241718080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Some fruit and vegetables you can collect: / way #2351 48.84, 61.81 - Ripe Bananas / way #2351 48.43, 61.41 - Ripe Coconuts / way #2351 48.78, 59.81 - Pine Apples / way #2351 47.20, 59.72 - Ripe Cabbages / way #2351 47.20, 59.72 - Ripe Tower Lettuce",
  "Wowhead050you have to walk backwards any direction after right clicking them to pull out the carrots and cabbages at least! talk about forgotten mechanics damn you can be a little bit faster if you move any direction pull back in the direction of another vegetable you can trip over in proximity to be able to start pulling the next one Last edited by Aubmaire on 2026/01/31 (Patch 12.0.0)",
  "Wowhead050Okay for Alliance try / way 39.64, 28.68 There's a Farm there where you can find ingredients",
  "Wowhead050Ugh. Can we *please* get rid of the quests where you pull something out of the ground and then get knocked on your ass? Pretty please.",
},

