[92576] = {
  "9257618080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050You are here because you can't find the last two banners. They are not in the yellow circled quest area. They are just to the south, Wayoint 55,36 and 52,36. UPDATE: 03/ 25/ 2026 Blizz updated the yellow quest circle to now include the two that were previously outside the quest area. Last edited by caldermi on 2026/03/25 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050All banners' locations, 8 possible, only 6 needed / way #2444 52.0, 30.7 / way #2444 52.0, 30.7 / way #2444 54.8, 20.8 / way #2444 55.2, 17.1 / way #2444 52.2, 17.2 / way #2444 54.8, 30.9 / way #2444 52.5, 20.9 / way #2444 54.3, 26.8 / way #2444 53, 26.8 Last edited by JonGhost52 on 2026/04/11 (Patch 12.0.1)",
},

[92577] = {
  "9257718080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050For Horde, use the teleport to Azsuna, then fly to Lorlathil, Val'sharah for a portal to Bel'ameth. The vendor is the innkeeper. Alliance has a direct Bel'ameth teleport in the Mage Sanctum. Last edited by Neridris on 2025/12/10 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050Do not go into the Emerald Dream for this. It's in the same location, but outside the dream.",
  "Wowhead050There's a portal direct to Belameth in the SW portal room",
  "Wowhead050I don't see anything anywhere, there is a quest indicator in the ground but no npc.",
  "Wowhead050Ok folks, I know there have been people like me who were getting frustrated not seeing Ellandrieth to complete this quest. Check to see if you have completed the Auspicious Gathering. You should be able to use this link to check: / run print(C_QuestLog.IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(77329)) If you get a false, then you need to complete this quest line in order to move forward with Dreamy Inspiration. I hope this helps because i was losing my ever loving mind. lol",
  "Wowhead050It is outside the portal - just fly over. Luckily you don't need to have unlocked the Emerald Dream zone to buy this. If you have never done any of the Dragonflight campaign, you can complete the very short intro quest from the capital city to reach the Dragon Isles and fly over. However, you will need 10x Dragon Isle supplies. They are Warband transferrable. You should manage to get this on your intro quest by clicking objects around the first zone.",
  "Wowhead050After reading comments here I was still confused. I have a HORDE character. Hopefully I can clarify what others have posted. First, take the portal from Orgrimmar to Valdrakken on the Dragon Isles. Next take the flight path from Valdrakken to Shady Sanctuary on the Ohn'ahran Plains. From the Shady Sanctuary you are going to fly West where the portal to the Emerald Dream is. Do not enter the Emerald Dream. You should see a quest called \"Auspicious Gathering\" with an exclamation on your map. There you will talk to a meeting of dragons and follow the questline, talking to Tyrande and serving food, etc. Once you have completed the quests in the area, the map will change to show Bel'ameth. In Bel'ameth there is a two story building. On the bottom floor is the NPC Ellandrieth. She has the item that you need to complete the quest. I hope this helps.",
  "Wowhead050Definitely NOT in the Emerald Dream. If you go to Valdrakken and portal to the Emerald Dream, fly out and then fly OVER the portal towards the marker on the map. It looks like a night elf village and Ellandrieth will be right there with the item.",
  "Wowhead050Not sure if anyone else did this, but I bought the Filigree Moon Lamp in Bel'ameth, then I added it to my house collection (before turning in the quest). The quest indicated that I purchased it and to return to Orgrimmar to turn it in. When I went to turn in the quest back in Orgrimmar, the quest reset as if I didn't buy it. Apparently the quest bugs out if you add the item to your collection before turn in.",
  "Wowhead050Ok. If you walk into the area and there isn’t a pretty big two story house with the inn keeper and the general goods vendor inside in that area. Make sure you’ve completed more of the campaign line for the emerald dream stuff. That was my issue. I had gotten everything just to the moon well activation apparently and decided to get side tracked without finishing the release of the spirits. So for me that whole area where it wants you to go to get the item was just blank spot next to a tree with a few tents and no one will talk to you. And when you are outside of the emerald dream in that area the vendors that are there don’t have the item.",
  "Wowhead050No one mentioned that you need to have dragon isle supplies to purchase this. I have not been able to transfer the supplies and the character in war within has not done dragon isles.",
  "Wowhead050If you can't see the vendor you probably haven't finished the Dragonflights after Amirdrasil quest chain on this character. Hope it becomes skippable and warbound soon. but as it is the quest chain takes about 10 mins to do it and the starting quest is near : / way 80, 48 East side of the zone right at the edge of the map Last edited by rainerpm on 2025/12/27 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050So to be able to see this vendor, you need to pick up a quest called \" A CHANGE LAND\", which is on the island, but in the outside phase. When you get the achievment \"Defenders of the Dream,\" you will be able to see the vendor.",
  "Wowhead050Previous: Furniture Favor Next: Draconic Decor Last edited by Eillesthis on 2026/02/11 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050I had to do three quests to get the vendor to show for me. A different Enthusiasm A Disquieting Feeling. Andu-falah-or Once I did those three the village showed for me. Took about 10 minutes or less to do all three.",
},

[92578] = {
  "9257818080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Vendor / way #2112 58.0 35.6 Unatos Last edited by Shardsy on 2025/12/27 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050[Draconic Decor] buy a draconic sconce - from the renown vendor Unatos by the inside stairs in Valdrackken, has 4 other decor items to buy. [Spare A Chair] travel to Mechagon, using the device you just got... go up the path to the Prince.. by the meeting stone.. buy from the Stolen Royal Vendorbot, several other items some need rep to buy. [Last Light] get nightborne lantern from the wretched First Arcanist Thalyssra inside the cave by the taxi Meredil, Suramar, Broken Isle. has several other rep needed items.",
  "Wowhead050Previous: Dreamy Inspiration Next: Spare A Chair Last edited by Eillesthis on 2026/02/11 (Patch 12.0.1)",
},

[92580] = {
  "9258018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050FYI, If you are Horde and used the teleporter option you will be teleported to the Alliance camp and immediately attacked by level 80 elites. It does NOT pvp flag you though. Someone needs to fix their teleporter scrolls.",
  "Wowhead050This quest offered by Second Chair Pawdo gives you Unstable Mechagon Re-Localizatron to use if you haven't unlocked Mechagon, though it's still faster to use it either way. You will need 10 Spare Parts to buy the required item from Stolen Royal Vendorbot , they drop from mobs around Mechagon. -- What follows is not required for completing this quest. It's a simple guide for new players to unlock Mechagon as it's likely Blizzard is doing those decor breadcrumb quests for discovery -- Alliance 1.a) Start A Dying World by talking to Earthen Guardian in Boralus. Just take the portal to the zone, no need to complete Bfa introduction. 1.b) If this quest isn't here, visit Silithus and directly and talk to Magni Bronzebeard . It needs to be Silithus BfA so talk to Zidormi to phase yourself properly if you don't see Magni. 2) Do the questline until you get Heart of Azeroth . 3) Do Send the Fleet in Boralus sending you to Nazjatar. Do the introduction quests until you unlock world quests. Doing Uniting Kul Tiras may be required for this step, which is getting three reputations to friendly (see quest). 4) Do The Legend of Mechagon in Boralus. 5) You should have unlocked Mechagon and can access it for good without this quest's item. Horde 1.a) Start A Dying World by talking to Earthen Guardian in Dazar'alor. Just take the portal to the zone, no need to complete Bfa introduction. 1.b) If this quest isn't here, visit Silithus and directly and talk to Magni Bronzebeard . It needs to be Silithus BfA so talk to Zidormi to phase yourself properly if you don't see Magni. 2) Do the questline until you get Heart of Azeroth . 3) Do Send the Fleet in Zul'Dazar sending you to Nazjatar. Do the introduction quests until you unlock world quests. Doing Uniting Zandalar may be required for this step, which is getting three reputations to friendly (see quest). 4) Do The Legend of Mechagon in Zul'Dazar. 5) You should have unlocked Mechagon and can access it for good without this quest's item. Last edited by Neridris on 2025/12/23 (Patch 11.2.7)",
  "Wowhead050If you need spare parts to buy the item for the quest, simpy fly up to Junkwatt Depot kill a mechanical mob and loot, you will get plenty spare parts to purchase the Bolt Chair.",
  "Wowhead050Previous: Draconic Decor Next: Last Light Last edited by Eillesthis on 2026/02/13 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050If you picked up an account-wide Neighborhood quest from Second Chair Pawdo and previously bought the quest item, you MIGHT not need to go buy another one. The reason I said MIGHT is because I was unsuccessful in replicating what I just did. Here's what happened: Picked up Spare A Chair on Horde Toon A in Orgrimmar then logged off. Just a minute later, I logged onto Horde Toon B who was in Dornogal. When Toon B went to Second Chair Pawdo in Dornogal, the quest was ready for turn-in. I did not turn in the quest though because I wanted to test whether that result could be replicated. I tried logging onto more toons (both factions), visiting the questgiver (in all 3 cities - SW, Org, Dornogal) and tried abandoning the quest and picking it up again a couple times. Nothing worked. The quest was not ready for turn-in again. Anyway it's worth a shot if you ran out of the required currency to buy the quest item and/ or just don't feel like trekking somewhere you've already been to buy something you already bought.",
  "Wowhead050(Horde-never did the Mech quests) I did not get the Unstable Mechagon Re-Localizatron upon accepting the quest. I did take the Banshees Wail to Drustvar and then the flight point to Prospectus Bay in Mech. Talked to the vendor but needed 10 Spare Parts. So, killed some things, got the parts and got kicked out to the Mech where I had to start the questline when I went to turn them in. But Went back to Drustvar and flew over again. I was able to make the purchase.",
},

