[92608] = {
  "9260818080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050You have to stand in the circles that show up on the minimap and take a picture of 5 locations indicated by the the beam of light which you can't see until you use the Scoped Max Falcon Stealth Dragon 90 . Horde locations are: / way Razorwind Shores 54.88, 56.67 / way Razorwind Shores 61.25, 50.85 / way Razorwind Shores 49.16, 61.35 / way Razorwind Shores 46.01, 55.60 / way Razorwind Shores 58.93, 69.39 / way Razorwind Shores 51.68, 69.69 / way Razorwind Shores 64.67, 70.38 / way Razorwind Shores 42.92, 50.03 Alliance Locations are: / way Founder's Point 52.67, 37.77 / way Founder's Point 39.99, 29.96 / way Founder's Point 33.38, 28.66 / way Founder's Point 62.78, 38.32 / way Founder's Point 32.99, 46.96 / way Founder's Point 44.64, 57.24 / way Founder's Point 58.03, 64.51 / way Founder's Point 63.39, 77.80 Last edited by DeadGilder on 2026/03/20 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Maybe I'm being negative, but I would have preferred a bit more choice in what photos to take instead of just being designated by the quest. -update- Just did this the second day and they're all the same locations? Is this actually intended or is it bugged? I get it's a daily that's supposed to be repeatable, that's what they always have been, but the exact same locations every time? Last edited by Jeolene on 2026/03/03 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Alliance Areas photo #1 / way Founder's Point 52.59, 37.99 photo #2 / way Founder's Point 62.81, 38.41 (facing water) photo #3 / way Founder's Point 58.15, 65.10 (fountain) photo #4 / way Founder's Point 63.36, 78.38 (facing west to the ocean) photo #5 / way Founder's Point 44.68, 57.30 (facing east)",
  "Wowhead050The photo spots are all around the map, not just in town. When you get near a spot where a photo needs to be taken, it shows a circle on the map. When you equip the camera, you see a huge blue arrow pointing down on the spot where the picture must be taken. If you get it right, the arrow goes away.",
  "Wowhead050Just click on the little circle with the arrows around it on your quest log to highlight the quest. Now there will be a guide arrow on your minimap guiding you to the nearest location that's part of the quest. Go there and you'll see a circle on the minimap. Stand in the circle and equip the camera (right-click it from inventory), and you'll see a shaft of light with a blue arrow pointing down. Aim at that and click the camera action button. Repeat as necessary to get the quest progress bar to 100%.",
  "Wowhead050I copied Olla's coords and got rid of the extra words, so it can be copied into paste / way Founder's Point 52.59, 37.99 / way Founder's Point 62.81, 38.41 (facing water) / way Founder's Point 58.15, 65.10 (fountain) / way Founder's Point 63.36, 78.38 (facing west to the ocean) / way Founder's Point 44.68, 57.30 (facing east)",
  "Wowhead050I've enjoyed the previous photography quests being steered around and allowed to take my own shots. But ugh, we're supposedly taking photos to inspire someone and have to robotically go to specific spots and take specific photos? How boring.",
  "Wowhead050I enjoy roaming around the neighbourhood, even did all the Lost Architect quests without help, but relatively speaking this is quite a bit of work for a mere three coupons and no house XP.",
  "Wowhead050If you don't have the camera in your inventory (for example if you took the quest on a different character), abandon and re-aquire the quest from the quest giver. I could not see a way to get him to give you another camera without doing this.",
  "Wowhead050\"you cant do that right now\" seriously? why do they have to complicate even something like this?",
  "Wowhead050Am I the only one that thinks this is kind of a lot of work for just 3 coupons? It just doesn't seem worth the time for me, lol.",
  "Wowhead050Make me fly all over to take \"inspiring\" photos? Fine. You get 5 pictures with the camera pointed straight down.",
  "Wowhead050an issue ive had with neighborhood quests is that it often sends me to the wrong neighborhood and this one is no different. completed it the first time (by going to the other neighborhood) but the 2nd time it doesnt give me the actual locations in either of the 2 and its so frustrating. these neighborhood quests are also often kinda tedious and take a while but give only 1-3 coupons? definitely doesnt feel worth it which is a shame because i thought wed have more reasons to be in the neighborhood but right now its better to just get things passively by doing current content without bothering much with these..",
  "Wowhead050This is just another example of Blizzard giving us crappy things to do with rewards that aren't worth the time spent doing them. \"Player Engagement\" for their stockholder's, slap in the face for their CUSTOMERS!",
},

[92617] = {
  "9261718080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050These are NOT inside the Grudge Pit, they are larger mobs found around the pit. Last edited by Shadelis on 2026/03/30 (Patch 12.0.1)",
},

[92657] = {
  "9265718080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050If you accept Stormarion Citadel quests before starting this one, Lysikas disappears. You have to abandon those for her to show back up. I'm currently stuck having completed those and don't know how to get her back.",
  "Wowhead050For those who are missing the NPC I believe the issue you're facing might be because you already taken/ completed the quest Tactical Acquisition . I need conformation on this though. You can just paste this command to chat in order to check if you have it completedit: / run print(C_QuestLog.IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(92658))",
  "Wowhead050Because no one has mentioned it here and for those like me trying to do the quest on your first 90: Will not show up till AFTER you finish the campaign for Voidstorm",
  "Wowhead050I am at 99% zone quest completion. No zone quests in my log. She is still not appearing. Not sure what else to try.",
  "Wowhead050I abandoned Voidstorm quests until she would finally appear",
  "Wowhead050So, I unknowingly progressed this questline and found the npc at / way 26.32, 68.36 NPC was at a different location as other comments pointed out already. Maybe it is of help to you, too. Last edited by Cirosh 15 days ago (Patch 12.0.5)",
  "Wowhead050This is a complete travesty. I have abandoned all my quests out there, I've finished the storyline quests, and NOTHING. I even submitted a ticket to Blizz and they told me to go to WoWhead because they don't give out answers to the quests. What a garbage dev team and company. This makes me want to cancel.",
},

