[93179] = {
  "9317918080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050These quests have such nice detail to flesh out the Amani. It's a little touching legend that a spirit will wait with the soul of a deceased child until their parents join them in the afterlife 😭",
  "Wowhead050The little pool is located at / way 51.52, 32.79 Don't mount up or you will lose the little guy! Last edited by Brotherben on 2026/03/05 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050I just did it as druid, and in druid flight form, i didnt loose it, i just flew over and dropped in the pool and got a achievement.",
  "Wowhead050\"You do not want to take the child back by force, but perhaps you can persuade her by to listen to you by helping her with what she is trying to accomplish here.\" FFS, blizz, did you let AI write this? Is it really that hard for people to proofread?",
},

[93180] = {
  "9318018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050If you cant see her make sure you meet her at / way 51.45, 30.63",
  "Wowhead050She dissapears after taking the quest.. just go to 50.8 31.4 and there she should be. The 2nd follow is the same it just closer so watch on map Last edited by Gaab on 2026/02/28 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050If after you kill the wasp enemies, and the \"?\" shows up back at the temple and she's not there (and the \"?\" disappears from your minimap when you get there) . . . fly north a little to where she was when she had you get the mushrooms. She'll be there and then ask you to go get a teapot. Last edited by josefu on 2026/02/28 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050/ way 50.77, 31.3 then / way 51.45, 30.63 for me",
  "Wowhead050I realize there are at least 3 separate posts with different waypoints that related to different parts of this quest. Those posts reference either Part 2, Part 3, or Part 6 of my post below. The purpose of this post is to gather and display a collection of those posts into a single post. Part 1: Picking up the quest. Kanza initially appears at / way #2437 52.29, 32.17 . Accept the quest. She WILL disappear. Part 2: She can be found at / way #2437 50.78, 31.42 . Talk to her again. She will run off and disappear again. Part 3: She should show up as a yellow dot on your minimap. But, if for some reason, she doesn't show up as a yellow dot, head to / way #2437 51.48, 30.60 . Part 4: Talk to her again to pick up some tasks to complete Part 5: Do the following tasks: 6 Stinger Hatchling slain (these will be the yellow non-aggressive wasp-like mobs) 4 Stinger Matriarch slain (these will be the aggressive wasp-like mobs) 20 Thorncap picked (each mushroom you pick will give between 4 and 5 Thorncaps) Part 6: Once done, the quest marker will tell you to go back to the temple. Don't. Instead head back to where you last saw her / way #2437 51.48, 30.60 . From there, everything is pretty straight forward. Last edited by eldiin on 2026/03/04 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050She kept disappearing when the quest was completed but finally appeared to turn the quest in at 51.46, 30.61",
  "Wowhead050She keeps disappearing the moment she runs away. I can't collect the mushrooms and killing the quest mobs does nothing.",
},

[93181] = {
  "9318118080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050I know I should talk to mama. but when I use my voice... all I hear is you. Hehehehehe I cried. Last edited by RomanVakarian on 2026/02/28 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050This quest line had no business in going for the heart strings like that ;-;",
  "Wowhead050I thought she just wanted to see the Loa... Man that was unexpected.",
  "Wowhead050Last time I got attacked by Onion Cutting Ninjas. I was doing the Darrowshire story line. Last edited by PrnJessus on 2026/03/04 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050You know what? It's my fault for having feelings.",
  "Wowhead050When I first entered Zul'Aman, I flew around and collected all the glyphs. I also stopped at the shrines I found and read their tablets. A loa for children! Surrounded by capybaras! He stays with children who have passed until their parents can collect them... I loved it, and I hoped it wasn't just environmental storytelling. Eversong's quests were pretty generic, and tbh disappointing -- there weren't any Windrunner sisters quests! But Zul'aman is really knocking it out of the park with these quests. This is the first time I've ever done ANY sojourner quests. I haven't bothered with them at all in previous expansions. And the main quest itself is SO satisfying. Whoever worked on these did a wonderful job.",
  "Wowhead050If, after all the quests are done, you happen to give Kanza a hug, she gives you a big raspberry sound back. But you know she's grateful for a friend. ;)",
  "Wowhead050Thanks Blizzard...I haven't teared up like that since DF quest with the old Dragonmaw orc.",
  "Wowhead050When little Kanza asks you to attend a tea party, you attend that tea party",
  "Wowhead050Thought I'd just get some side quests done..wasn't expecting such an emotional story. Wow.",
  "Wowhead050The last tea party we held in Drustvar was different...",
  "Wowhead050Just as over rated of a quest as the terrible one with the Earthen who had dementia and we needed to kill a whole forest's worth of animals to make a stupid lantern for.",
},

