[93573] = {
  "9357318080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Holy crap. I typically LOVE puzzle world quests and treasures like this, but this one took me way longer to figure out than it should have. In case anyone is confused on what to do: You are NOT trying to form any particular shape, like similar looking puzzles we've had in the past. Instead, you are trying to rearrange the dots so they are next to their 'buddy' dots. The lightning lines connecting them are there to tell you that those two dots want to be closer to each other. eg. If there is lightning connecting the 1st dot on the top row to the 3rd dot on the bottom row , you would want to click on the 3rd dot on the bottom row and swap it with either the 1st dot on the bottom row OR the 2nd dot on the top row . Rinse and repeat for all dots until all of the lines turn blue. Solid blue line = dot is next to the correct dot(s). It's tricky to explain, but once you understand it it's a super quick puzzle. Good luck!",
  "Wowhead050I'm too dumb for this *!@#",
  "Wowhead050The worst puzzle quest in the game. The old ones were fine.",
  "Wowhead050This is a BS world quest. Way too much time to spend on a puzzle, let alone 3 in a row. Whoever designed this can kick rocks.",
  "Wowhead050I'm too old for this *!@#",
  "Wowhead050fire whoever designed this, please...out of a cannon maybe Last edited by Butters140 on 2026/03/28 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Absolutely horrible.",
  "Wowhead050I'm too impatient for this &*!@",
  "Wowhead050Yeah, no. This sucks.",
  "Wowhead050From what I can understand the red/ blue lightning effect between nodes means they want to be close together. Use left-clicks or right clicks to select a node and another node to swap them. When they're close together it'll make a solid void line. You want to make all line solid void three times to finish the world quest.",
  "Wowhead050whom ever redesigned this off the fun triangles needs to be forced to do 3 of these in a row daily to unlock there vital items (car, house doors, lock to there epi-pen cabinet) ...Etc lmao can we get a mod that black lists this world quest!",
  "Wowhead050Does any review things before it is rolled, who WHO thought this was a good idea for a WQ? ead",
  "Wowhead050might be the worst designed world quest of all time",
  "Wowhead050I feel like someone at Blizzard took too seriously the criticism that the puzzles from The War Within being insultingly easy and overcompensated, I like that it's harder (I really like puzzles) but maybe not make us do it three times in a row if you want to amp up the difficulty.",
  "Wowhead050Didn't need more reasons to hate you Blizz. You gave me one anyway.",
  "Wowhead050Wasted 30 min on this. I was able to solve 2 of them by accident but stuck on the 3rd. It might be possible if there was some kinda of instruction on what you're actually supposed to be doing here. It sucks that there is gear locked behind this nonsense.",
  "Wowhead050I solved it by waiting a day for the puzzle to get rearranged into a non-square shape that made it trivial.",
  "Wowhead050man, whoever came up with this puzzle was a masochist! i manage to get through all 3. the top comment help a lot",
  "Wowhead050this is the puzzle/ quest would drive anyone to madness. no wonder so many npcs turn to the void...... the square puzzle is just unnecessarily complicated. more complicated does not mean better quest design, blizz. update: i solved the square puzzle. basically you want the orbs with 3 lines in the corners, 1 line each going to its neighbors and one line going into the middle orb. the orbs that are between corner-orbs have two lines each, and the orb that goes into the middle has four lines going back into the four corner orbs. hope this helps. Last edited by gyunikornis on 2026/03/29 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Try to get all the lines dark blue. Red lightning lines are bad. The red lines link nodes that are too far away from each other. Swap nodes to bring them closer together.",
  "Wowhead050To add to the pain, the dots are unresponsive to mouse clicks. Takes three to five attempts before they react. And, as usual, the game does not properly scale with the screen size. Edit: noticed that in the middle row one must click a bit AWAY from the dot. Last edited by MrsBean on 2026/03/29 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050Glad to see i'm not the only one who thinks this puzzle is a bit more complicated than what we're used to. What drove me mad however, is that 99% of the time the orbs don't react when you click on them.",
  "Wowhead050If you're having trouble clicking on these, the \"hitbox\" for the circles is actually slightly above them.",
},

