[94834] = {
  "9483418080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050This unlocks the Loa of Abundance, for use in the Altar of Blessings. The Altar of Blessings allows you to combine the blessings of one of the greater Loa, with one of the lesser Loa. The Loa of Abundance, when combined with: Akil'zon, Loa of Victory: Blessing: Abundant Rush - The loas of Victory and Abundance vastly increase your profession Gathering and Crafting speed by granting you +15 Deftness and +50 Crafting Speed. Halazzi, Loa of the Hunt: Blessing: Guide of the Harvest - The loas of the Hunt and Abundance bless your Professions Gathering with a 15% chance to summon a Visage of Dundun every time you successfully harvest using Mining, Herbalism, Skinning, or Fishing. Jan'alai, Loa of Fire: Blessing: Harvest Haste - The loas of the Hunt and Abundance increase your Movement Speed by 100% for 5 sec whenever you gather reagents via Mining, Herbalism, Skinning, or Fishing. Nalorakk, Loa of War: Blessing: Abundance Permanence - Whenever you gather reagents via Mining, Herbalism, Skinning, or Fishing, the Loas of War and Abundance heal you by 15% and reduce damage taken by 50% until you're damaged next. Note that this blessing is independent of the blessings of the major Loa. You can have, for instance, Nalorakk's blessing at the same time as the Abundant Rush blessing.",
  "Wowhead050You can buy it on a second char, while no longer able to accept the quest, and then you cannot vendor it anymore. 1600 points down the drain. That + the event being extremely bugged is a job well done, Blizzard.",
  "Wowhead050This quest unlocks Blessings of Abundance for your warband . Last edited by DarkShade on 2026/03/17 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050You can resell the item immediately after accepting the quest and you will get your currency back without losing the quest.",
},

[94839] = {
  "9483918080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050Got mine from fishing for the Quest A Fish! . Will send you to Du'gal deep in Zul'aman. Is a part of the Achievement Altar of Blessings: Amani Curious and also unlocks the Blessings of Peril . No followup quest. Last edited by Stepbrah on 2026/02/27 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050You can get this by fishing in ANY midnight zones. Pools or open water, doesn't matter. Skill required is very low (has been caught with fishing skill as low as ~40). Drop rate estimated around 0.5%, If you're farming specifically for it, I recommend using Amani Angler's Ward OR fishing at the Silvermoon pond so you won't be bothered by Blood Hunters. Required for Altar of Blessings: Amani Curious and Altar of Blessings: Sacred Buffet Devotee . Last edited by rhinoloupe on 2026/03/17 (Patch 12.0.1)",
  "Wowhead050just fished this up in silvermoon im like 112 midnight fishing all it does is ad a lesser loa you can choose from at the alter in zul' aman i only have this one unlocked for the lessers loas but this one seems very strong if you match it with the loa of the hunt you have a 25% chance to hit and deal 100% more dmg but you allso have a 25% chance to deal 50% less dmg... buff only active in Sul' Aman.",
  "Wowhead050Just fished this quest up in Eversong Woods.",
  "Wowhead050Here is my drop info Fishing Level: 125 Location: Silvermoon CIty Items used: Aqirite Fisherfriend & Angler's Anomaly",
  "Wowhead050Catched at 43.67 81.72 at first try, then only trash. a small pond in city fishing 91.",
  "Wowhead050I got this at Midnight fishing level 98, outside of Goldenmist Village in Eversong Woods. My fishing tool is a Strong Fishing Pole",
},

[94840] = {
  "9484018080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050From Idol of the Depths . You can refund the quest item after accepting the quest. Unlocks new blessings: Blessing: Victorious Waves Blessing: Devoted Adaptation Blessing: Buoyant Flame Blessing: War on the Currents Last edited by Durbaa 22 days ago (Patch 12.0.5)",
  "Wowhead050You can purchase it from Depthdiver Tu'nakit for 1500 Angler Pearls in Zul'Aman / way #2437 68.2 20.2 Depthdiver Tu'nakit",
},

[94844] = {
  "9484418080NPCUnknown0NPCUnknown00",
  "Wowhead050In case anyone else is as confused as I was - The item will not work if the mob is already buffed. When you use the item, it buffs the mob for 3 minutes and it gains a red aura. It cannot be rebuffed until the aura is gone. I was foolishly trying to buff mobs that already had the buff without realising and getting frustrated that it wasn't working.",
},

